# LF in the repository, everywhere, for every text file.
#
# Without this, src/page.js, scripts/smoke.mjs, scripts/cdp.mjs and three files under
# .ai-context/ drifted to CRLF on a Windows checkout and were committed that way, which turns
# any later diff of them into a whole-file rewrite: merging feature/date-range into develop
# reported 13556 insertions where the real change was 3861, and would have made `git blame`
# on this project's three main source files point at that one merge for every line.
#
# text=auto lets git decide what is text; eol=lf fixes what it writes for the files it decides
# are. The binary lines below are belt and braces -- detection already gets these right, but
# these files are the ones where a wrong guess would corrupt the artefact rather than annoy a
# reviewer, and the hero webp and the screenshots are what a release ships.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.webp binary
